{"type":"text","timestamp":1794534256036,"sessionID":"ses_e2d72f59fffei31JMJu7HhMOUx","part":{"id":"prt_1d293955a002FlMkn6kQxxiQlN","sessionID":"ses_e2d72f59fffei31JMJu7HhMOUx","messageID":"msg_1d29378f9001UWnFF77LC4UF28","type":"text","text":"T007 is implemented and verified. Here is the report.\n\n## Files written\n\n**`/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.ts`** (the only tracked file I changed)\n- Added `export const PROMPT_EMBEDDING_DEADLINE_MS = 750` in the constants section.\n- Added `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError` (its `name` is the required string) in the prompt-embedding section.\n- In `withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding`, the `adapter.embed([prompt], { inputType: 'query' })` call now runs `embedding.catch(() => undefined)` and is raced against a deadline timer that rejects with `PromptEmbeddingTimeoutError`. The timer is cleared in a `finally`.\n\n**Generated (gitignored, no tracked files):** `dist/` from `npm --prefix $ADV run build`, needed because the capture refuses to run against a stale `dist` and only reads the compiled scorer.\n\n## Verify output\n\n1. `npm --prefix $ADV run typecheck` → `exit=0`\n```\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\n```\n\n2. `npx vitest run tests/scorer` (from `$ADV`) → 0 failed\n```\n Test Files  37 passed (37)\n      Tests  348 passed | 2 skipped (350)\n```\n\n3. `node $C | $M` → exactly the T001 default-capture numbers\n```\n{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}\n{\"tune\":{\"own\":2,\"attached\":7,\"combined\":9,\"total\":45},\"holdout\":{\"own\":0,\"attached\":0,\"combined\":0,\"total\":44}}\n{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- The first capture attempt exited with `@spec-kit/system-skill-advisor dist is stale`. This was pre-existing (dist built 02:33, source edits after), not caused by the final source state. I ran `npm --prefix $ADV run build` so the capture could exercise the compiled scorer. That build writes only gitignored output, but it is outside T007's named line. T031 must rebuild after all wave edits anyway. If a build is meant to be orchestrator-only, this is the deviation to note.\n- I did not tick the T007 checkbox, did not commit, and left every other worker's file untouched.","time":{"start":1794534249818,"end":1794534256036}}}
